# Originally converted from sike_sandals.glb by tools/models/glb_tool.py.
# ⚠️ THAT TOOL NO LONGER EXISTS IN THE REPO, so this file is now maintained by hand.
# Re-running the converter would reintroduce the bug below; edit here instead.
#
# ⚠️ m2 IS THE SHOE BODY AND ITS Kd MUST NOT GO BACK TO 0 0 0.
# The source GLB ships baseColorFactor [0,0,0,1] on both body materials and carries no
# textures at all, so the converter faithfully wrote pure black. A pure-black albedo
# returns nothing under the toon key light: every curve on the upper resolves to the same
# value and the shoe renders as a flat silhouette with the m3 swoosh floating on top.
# That is the "IKE is corrupted" report. The mesh itself is clean (33,856 unique
# positions, 0 degenerate faces, normals and UVs present) so the geometry needs nothing.
#
# 0.052/0.058/0.074, HALVED FROM 0.105/0.115/0.145 ON 2026-08-29.
# 🧑 asked twice in one sitting: "make sike darker too", then "sike/ike still aint dark enough".
#
# ⚠️ THE OLD NUMBER'S REASONING WAS NOT WRONG, ITS CONDITIONS CHANGED. It was measured as
# "the darkest the body can sit and still separate the toe box from the midsole" against a
# 0.012 m prop ink border. That border is 0.006 m as of the same day (ToonSkin.PropOutlineWidth,
# docs/TODO.md § 78.7), so twice as much of the shoe's own shading is now visible and the
# separation it was protecting no longer depends on the albedo being that light.
#
# ⚠️ STILL NOT ZERO, AND IT MUST NOT GO THERE. The floor is the original bug: a pure black
# albedo returns nothing under the toon key light, every curve resolves to one value, and the
# shoe becomes a flat silhouette with the m3 swoosh floating on it. That is the "IKE is
# corrupted" report and 0 0 0 is what caused it. This is dark, not black.
newmtl m2
Kd 0.05200 0.05800 0.07400
Ks 0.14000 0.14000 0.16000
Ns 48.00000
d 1.00000
illum 2
newmtl m3
Kd 0.94000 0.94000 0.93000
Ks 0.08000 0.08000 0.08000
Ns 24.00000
d 1.00000
illum 2
